":3},"1894781eb0be0be65b8e":{"type":"paragraph","text":"In this age of technology, many young people obtain much of the information they need from online viewing materials. Such materials mostly come from Youtube, Instagram, and Snapchat—the most popular online platforms among teens based on a new Pew Research Center Survey (Anderson and Jiang, 2018).","bbox":[72.0,587.510009765625,526.5099487304688,642.2900390625],"page":3},"a8ac64c16591c8ef824e":{"type":"paragraph","text":"As a student, you must enhance your capacity to filter information obtained from such sources. It will make you avoid misinformation, which has recently become prevalent due to fake news. You also need to sharpen your skill in judging the relevance and worth of their content before using them as bases for personal decisions, especially when dealing with social issues, concerns in real life.","bbox":[72.0,650.7100219726562,526.6859741210938,719.300048828125],"page":3},"c793e3350083c1528106":{"type":"paragraph","bbox":[72.0,120.72003173828125,524.4111515925481,148.32000732421875],"text":"In making sound judgments about the overall quality of information presented \nin a viewing material, you need to consider the following elements: ","page":4},"ee326bf1a945d4755687":{"type":"paragraph","text":"1. Relevance: the information's level of importance to a particular viewing","bbox":[90.0250015258789,156.56004333496094,526.7059936523438,169.94004821777344],"page":4},"9a9778685dae38ebb6ff":{"type":"paragraph","text":"purpose or explicitly stated need for that information","bbox":[90.0250015258789,170.3600311279297,526.5218505859375,211.3400115966797],"page":4},"2783c1084fef68977e01":{"type":"paragraph","bbox":[88.5250015258789,197.82000732421875,524.4111515925481,308.23004150390625],"text":"2. Accuracy: the extent to which information contains factual and updated details \nthat can be verified by consulting alternative and/or primary sources \n \n3. Bias/Perspective: the position or slant toward which an author shapes \ninformation \n \n4. Reliability: the information's level of trustworthiness based on information \nabout the author and the publishing body ","page":4},"6b6713f92639285126ef":{"type":"figure","bbox":[128.89999389648438,251.5,466.3999938964844,589.0],"src":"/assets/curriculum/figures/9c724351983a6b3fb728c2f9.webp","text":"","width":300,"height":300,"page":4},"d52080d6b7373ef0af30":{"type":"heading","text":"References:","bbox":[72.0,329.0600280761719,144.0659942626953,342.44000244140625],"page":4},"3a10556d46789d044a22":{"type":"paragraph","text":"1. https://www.edutopia.org/blog/evaluating-quality-of-online-info-julie-coiro\n2. https://www.pewresearch.org/internet/2018/05/31/teens-social-media-","bbox":[90.0250015258789,349.8900451660156,502.4159851074219,377.0460205078125],"page":4},"2fe447d888df7335bab5":{"type":"paragraph","text":"technology-2018/ Activities","bbox":[72.0,377.49005126953125,203.46600341796875,418.3700256347656],"page":4},"daffe0bb826d7a6773a7":{"type":"paragraph","text":"A. Directions: Study the given situation, then identify the element it highlights.","bbox":[79.5,424.7900390625,505.1059875488281,438.1700134277344],"page":4},"1a9f9b7ceb24a37bf915":{"type":"paragraph","text":"_________ 1. Mario pays attention to the source of the material he watches. He wants to","bbox":[72.0,440.7799987792969,525.8982543945312,545.5599975585938],"page":4},"24824e6ed831dff67a43":{"type":"heading","text":"a. Accuracy c. Relevance","bbox":[158.8300018310547,468.09002685546875,418.1860046386719,481.4700012207031],"page":4},"044b5a15828875da7786":{"type":"heading","text":"b. Bias/Perspective d. Reliability","bbox":[158.8300018310547,488.7900390625,376.885986328125,502.1700134277344],"page":4},"6f6cef32d0d0c2c53dcc":{"type":"paragraph","text":"confirm the credibility of its creator before believing any information it contains. _________ 2. Sonia evaluates the content of the materials she consults to determine whether","bbox":[72.0,545.9949951171875,526.4000244140625,596.1799926757812],"page":4},"9411fd2c6319ded1af8d":{"type":"paragraph","text":"they directly address her need for information. _________ 3. Dennis check on the sources cited in the video to see whether the data provided","bbox":[72.0,596.614990234375,526.2310791015625,634.1799926757812],"page":4},"1b9531700fad8d33bd93":{"type":"paragraph","text":"are accurate. _________ 3. Linda does not entirely believe that the content of materials favoring one thing,","bbox":[72.0,634.5150146484375,526.4299926757812,672.0800170898438],"page":4},"0c5404901544954b5f3c":{"type":"paragraph","bbox":[153.02999877929688,659.4700317382812,524.4111515925481,684.77001953125],"text":"_________ 3.  Linda does not entirely believe that the content of materials favoring one thing, \nperson, or group over another, especially in a way considered unfair. ","page":4},"61e40cfc9b639ae7cb46":{"type":"paragraph","text":"person, or group over another, especially in a way considered unfair.","bbox":[72.0,672.4149780273438,490.03802490234375,753.5950317382812],"page":4},"983621a2656a5f04be9f":{"type":"paragraph","bbox":[154.19232177734375,98.405029296875,523.3800048828125,128.6199951171875],"text":"B. Directions: Watch the video, then evaluate the material using the \ngiven rubric. ","page":5},"f482312a489ab0764e89":{"type":"paragraph","text":"B. Directions: Watch the video, then evaluate the material using the","bbox":[135.02999877929688,99.13999938964844,526.58203125,112.5199966430664],"page":5},"cf07ab63c676f37f5ea4":{"type":"paragraph","text":"given rubric.","bbox":[153.02000427246094,115.06004333496094,221.75599670410156,128.44004821777344],"page":5},"d12e78b4018963cbcbaf":{"type":"figure","bbox":[104.5999984741211,140.20001220703125,491.5,379.3000183105469],"src":"/assets/curriculum/figures/95b3a0ca1748fc9214d65988.webp","text":"","width":898,"height":605,"page":5,"transcript":"youtube.com/watch?v=s_6QW9sNPEY"},"dc2b7f423003aa83f24f":{"type":"figure","bbox":[128.89999389648438,251.